'' ' 3  3  1  1  1  1  1  2  5  5  6  7  4  4'. The first draft of the rule refused the
'' NULL POINTER CONSTANT -- 'cptr( any ptr, 0 )' to a number -- which is what the
'' vendored numbers/cast-nullptr.bas writes twenty times; a corpus sweep found it.
''
'' NOT ASSERTED: '0 statements not lowered'. Lines 50 and 51 -- the null constant to a
'' number -- were already dropped before this rule (lowerctl.bas:213, the call scores
'' unviable), and still are. That is a missing conversion, not a diagnostic, and this
'' test is about the diagnostic.
